## Async / Await Rules

```csharp
// Correct
await _userService.GetUserAsync(userId, cancellationToken);

// Wrong
_userService.GetUserAsync(userId).Result;
_userService.GetUserAsync(userId).Wait();
```

- Use plain `await` — do NOT use `.ConfigureAwait(false)`
- WebAPI controller actions: include `CancellationToken cancellationToken` when downstream calls are cancellable
- BackgroundService / Worker: use `stoppingToken` from `ExecuteAsync` and propagate through all async operations
- Always propagate the active token through Service → Provider; do not drop or replace it
- Keep async style consistent with surrounding project files

---

## Logging Rules

```csharp
// Correct — method name + key identifier
_logger.Log(LogLevel.Error, $"[{nameof(GetUser)}] user not found: {userId}");
_logger.Log(LogLevel.Error, $"[{nameof(CreateOrder)}] DB write failed: Order, create");

// Wrong
Console.WriteLine("user not found");
_logger.Log(LogLevel.Error, "error");  // no context
```

- Log external API failures: include request name and response code
- Log DB write failures: include entity name and operation type
- Do NOT log full request payload if it may contain sensitive data

