## Code Style

- Use file-scoped namespaces if already used in the repo
- Use primary constructors only if already used in the repo
- Keep methods small and focused
- Prefer explicit types for service boundaries and models
- Add comments only for non-obvious business rules

---

## Self-Check for Service Files

Before finishing, verify:
- [ ] No raw SQL / DB calls?
- [ ] No raw `HttpClient` calls?
- [ ] No injection of another Service?
- [ ] `[DependencyInjection]` on implementation, Singleton lifetime?
- [ ] `await` used (not `.Result` / `.Wait()`)?
- [ ] CancellationToken propagated through all async calls?
- [ ] Logging includes method name and business identifier?
- [ ] New/modified private methods use camelCase; private fields use `_camelCase` (see `naming.mdc`)?
